Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.32 phase 2: marker list, area-name readback and a test aid for the new full-screen map

P6.32 phase 2 (docs/P6.32_MAP_ZOOM.md section 14). Patch 0146 gives the new screen
the spots' positions, the visited flags and the reveal pieces; this one adds the rest
of what the screen needs, all read from the game's own tables and never written back:

- mapViewData (every frame while the screen is available): the marker list (every
  spot's frame, x and y; every town's x and y and whether the list for the game's
  progress shows it), the current area (STSTATUS_areaFuncs.getArea(), its spot is
  area + 1), and the area names' file and the language (the EU disc has one copy of
  each text file per language: TEXT_FILE() carries it).
- mapViewName (every frame while the screen is open, right after the game's own
  STSTATUS_showMapArea ran on the view's cursor): reads back what the name window
  holds (the table's string for the spot under the cursor, as font codes and as
  Shift-JIS codes through the game's glyph map, a line break as 0x0A), the width the
  game measures for it, the window's place, and whether the window's text is the
  table's string for that spot. The host logs one line per name shown with this.
- mapViewForceAreas: test aid, PC only, like DW3_FORCE_CARDS of patch 0100.
  DW3_FORCE_MAP_AREAS=all (or <first>-<last>, spot ids 1..46) marks those areas
  visited so a replay can put the cursor on every named location. Unset (every release,
  and the Switch) it does nothing.

With the option file key map_screen off (the default) or widescreen off nothing here
runs: dw3_port_map_view_wants() is 0 and the Map screen is the one of patch 0080.

